# White Chicken Chili

Based on [https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/…](https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1024345-white-chicken-chili) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251214090115/https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1024345-white-chicken-chili))

{ rating="5" image="white_chicken_chili.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Soup

- [ ] 1 large [yellow onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, chopped
- [ ] 1 large [jalapeño pepper]{ ing="jalapeno-pepper" }, seeds and ribs removed, finely chopped
- [ ] 2 Tbsps [minced garlic]{ ing="minced-garlic" } (about 5 cloves)
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }, to taste
- [ ] 1 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, plus more to taste (such as Diamond Crystal)
- [ ] Freshly [cracked black pepper]{ ing="cracked-black-pepper" }
- [ ] 4 cups [low-sodium chicken broth]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken-broth" }
- [ ] 2 (15-ounce) cans [cannellini beans]{ ing="cannellini-beans" }, rinsed and drained
- [ ] 2 (4-ounce) cans [diced green chiles]{ ing="diced-green-chiles" }
- [ ] 2.5-3 cups [cooked shredded chicken]{ ing="cooked-shredded-chicken" } (follow the recipe to poach 1.5-1.75 lbs or from a rotisserie chicken)
- [ ] 1 cup fresh or [frozen corn kernels]{ ing="frozen-corn-kernels" }
- [ ] Half a [lime]{ ing="lime" }, plus lime wedges for serving

### For Serving (optional)

- [ ] [Shredded Cheddar]{ ing="shredded-cheddar" } or Monterey Jack cheese
- [ ] [Pickled jalapeño slices]{ ing="pickled-jalapeno-slices" }
- [ ] [Diced avocado]{ ing="diced-avocado" }
- [ ] [Sour cream]{ ing="sour-cream" }
- [ ] [Chopped fresh cilantro]{ ing="chopped-fresh-cilantro" }
- [ ] [Crushed tortilla chips]{ ing="crushed-tortilla-chips" }

## Recipe

1. In a large Dutch oven, heat the olive oil over medium heat

   1. Add the onion and jalapeño and cook, stirring often, until the [onions]{ ing="yellow-onion" } are tender, about 6 minutes
   1. Add the [garlic]{ ing="minced-garlic" }, [oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, paprika, cayenne, [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } and a few grinds of [black pepper]{ ing="cracked-black-pepper" }, and cook for 1 minute, until fragrant
1. Add the [chicken broth]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken-broth" }, [cannellini beans]{ ing="cannellini-beans" }, and [diced green chiles]{ ing="diced-green-chiles" } with their liquid; bring to a boil over medium-high heat

   1. Lower the heat and simmer, stirring occasionally, until the broth has reduced by about half, 18-20 minutes
   1. Off the heat, use a wooden spoon to mash some of the beans against the side of the pot. Continue mashing the beans until the broth is noticeably thicker
1. Return the pot to medium, stir in the [chicken]{ ing="cooked-shredded-chicken" } and corn, and cook until heated through, about 3 minutes

   1. Juice the [lime]{ ing="lime" } half over the pot, then taste for seasonings and add more salt, black pepper, and cayenne, if desired
1. Serve the chili in bowls with recommended toppings
